   "frases": [
    {
     "es": "Había una giganta llamada Nótt, la Noche, oscura como toda su familia.",
     "en": "There was a giantess named Nott, the Night, dark like all her family."
    },
    {
     "es": "Odín le dio un caballo negro, Hrímfaxi, y un carro para cruzar el cielo.",
     "en": "Odin gave her a black horse, Hrimfaxi, and a chariot to cross the sky."
    },
    {
     "es": "La espuma del freno del caballo cae a la tierra como rocío. Por eso la hierba amanece mojada.",
     "en": "Foam from the horse's bit falls to earth as dew. That is why the grass is wet in the morning."
    },
    {
     "es": "Su hijo era Dagr, el Día. Odín le dio un caballo brillante, Skinfaxi, cuya crin ilumina el mundo.",
     "en": "Her son was Dagr, the Day. Odin gave him a bright horse, Skinfaxi, whose mane lights up the world."
    },
    {
     "es": "Así, una tras otro, la Noche y el Día cruzan el cielo y le dan la vuelta al mundo.",
     "en": "So, one after the other, Night and Day ride across the sky and circle the world."
    }
